T*
(Corvan Grain: October sea shipments down 62% on last year) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] Corvan Grain reports that its sea shipments of wheat and maize in October) Tj
T*
(2026 were 62% below the same month a year earlier.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] The fall follows the end of the Corridor Agreement on 10 September and the) Tj
T*
(strike at Orvan Grain Port that began on 14 September.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The company has moved some cargoes to the Ravik Rail Link and to road) Tj
T*
(haulage. Rail capacity is limited and cannot replace the sea route.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] "We are shipping what we can and telling buyers the truth about the rest,") Tj
T*
(a company spokesperson said.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The statement is unusual for the firm, which normally leaves monthly) Tj
T*
(figures to the trade press. A spokesperson said the company wanted to correct) Tj
T*
(what it called exaggerated accounts of the disruption. The company has not) Tj
T*
(changed its contracts with Midgard or Tolan buyers, and it says it is honouring) Tj
T*
(them where shipping allows. It has also warned that the rail alternative is) Tj
T*
(expensive and that some cargoes will arrive late. The firm will not give a) Tj
T*
(forecast for the first quarter.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The company's statement does not give a monthly breakdown by product, and) Tj
T*
(it does not say how much of the fall is due to the strike rather than the end of) Tj
T*
(the agreement. It says both mattered. The figures are for its own shipments, not) Tj
T*
(for the port as a whole.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] Corvan Grain will publish its November figures in the normal cycle.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
